---
description: Anti-patterns that must never be introduced in ProjectX
alwaysApply: true
---

# Forbidden Patterns

If you recognize any pattern below, **do not implement it**. Use the referenced rule or ADR instead.

## Tenant & data

- ❌ Direct `mongoose.connection.useDb()` in controllers — use `getTenantModel` / model routing.
- ❌ Trusting `tenantId`, `tenantDbName`, or subdomain from request body/query to select DB.
- ❌ Cross-tenant queries or emits without `tenantDbName` in room/event options.
- ❌ Disabling cookie/header tenant mismatch checks.

## Auth & security

- ❌ Skipping `VerifyJwt` on protected REST routes or upload/download handlers.
- ❌ Storing refresh tokens in `localStorage` (web) or `AsyncStorage` (mobile).
- ❌ New parallel login/session stacks instead of extending `JWTProvider` / `AuthContext`.
- ❌ Committing `.env`, Firebase admin SDK JSON, or service account keys.

## Files

- ❌ Public unauthenticated access to `/uploads/*` in production.
- ❌ Filesystem reads using unsanitized client paths (must use `path.basename`, allowed categories).

## Frontend & mobile

- ❌ Hardcoded hex/rgb colors when `--ax-*` or Shadcn tokens exist.
- ❌ Duplicate axios instances — use `setupAxios` (web) or `httpClient` (mobile).
- ❌ Heavy business logic, permission checks, or tenant resolution inside JSX components.
- ❌ Polling aggressively when Socket.IO is connected.

## Database & jobs

- ❌ Unbounded `find()` without `limit`/pagination on list endpoints or jobs.
- ❌ Sequential `await` in loops over large recipient/tenant lists when batching is possible.
- ❌ Scheduler/reminder jobs without explicit `runWithTenantContext(tenantDbName, ...)`.
- ❌ Non-idempotent cron jobs that duplicate notifications on retry.

## Realtime

- ❌ Socket connections without JWT + tenant resolution (mirror HTTP policy).
- ❌ Emitting to global `user:{id}` rooms when `tenantDbName` is known — use `tenant:{db}:user:{id}`.
- ❌ Duplicate `useRealtimeEvent` subscriptions for the same event without cleanup.
